/Alt (A three-panel line chart showing different potential drivers of the neutral rate. Each panel shows a different possible driver over 1990 to 2025. The top panel shows the working age population relative to the old-age population in the OECD has declined steadily over time. The middle panel shows that productivity growth in the OECD declined notably in the 200s and remains relatively slow. The bottom panel shows that inequality in the United States \(represented by the Gini Index\) has increased over time.)
/K 1
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
