/Alt (Two-panel graph comparing the Brent crude oil price with gasoline, diesel and jet fuel prices between 2018 and 2026. The Brent crude oil price rises sharply in 2022, falls, then rises again in 2026 and is elevated at the last datapoint around $110 US per barrel. Gasoline, diesel and jet fuel prices move broadly together, similarly rising sharply in 2022 and 2026. All three prices are elevated at the end point at price levels above the brent crude oil price.)
/K 14
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
