/Alt (Line chart comparing prices for eight agricultural commodities: wheat, soybeans, palm oil, corn, sugar, cotton, cocoa and coffee. Prices generally rise and become more volatile over the period, although movements differ considerably across commodities. Wheat records the strongest rise among the upper group before falling back, while soybeans remain relatively elevated and palm oil and corn finish lower. Among the lower group, sugar and cotton rise overall, cocoa falls sharply early before recovering, and coffee fluctuates considerably and finishes comparatively low.)
