/Alt (Two-panel line chart showing housing prices indexed to their pre-downturn peak \(=100\), in nominal terms \(left\) and real terms \(right\), from 24 months before the peak to about 36 months after. The shaded area shows the range across previous downturns, and the line shows the current cycle. In both panels, prices in the current cycle rose into the peak and have since declined for six months. In nominal terms, prices have fallen about 5 per cent from the peak, to around 95, which is within the range of previous downturns but has been relatively steep. In real terms, prices have fallen about 6 per cent, to around 94, which is towards the middle of the historical range.)
