/Alt (A one-panel graph showing the model average of model estimates of the unemployment gap with a swath reflecting the highest and lowest bounds of the one-standard-error confidence intervals across the selection of models. It shows that the central range of model estimates for the unemployment gap has seen only modest easing in recent years and remains tight. The graph also shows estimates of labour market tightness based on the median indicator of the suite of labour market indicators, as well as a swath that shows the range of indicators. It shows that the median indicator suggests a little less tightness than the model-based estimates, but continues to suggest that labour market conditions are a little tight. A blue dot indicates the partial estimates of the median indicator for the September quarter 2026 that continues to indicate some tightness in the labour market.)
/K 23
