/Alt (A quarterly line graph showing liaison measures of year-ended growth in current and expected wages, compared with year-ended growth in the private sector Wage Price Index. The time series start in 2004, and since then the liaison measures and the Wage Price Index measure have closely tracked each other, albeit with periods of divergence. The liaison measure of current wages growth has picked up since mid-2026 to be around 3.8 per cent in the September quarter, compared with closer to 3 per cent at the start of the year. Similarly, the liaison measure of expected wages growth has increased from around 3.2 per cent at the start of 2026 to around 3.6 per cent in the September quarter. By contrast, the Wage Price Index series was around 3.1 per cent in the June quarter \(the most recent available data point\).)
/K 1
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
>>
