/A 2201 0 R
/Alt (A two-panel line-bar graph decomposing the deviations in the forecast for quarterly trimmed mean inflation growth from a rate consistent with the midpoint of the target range. The top panel shows the central forecasts and is identical to Graph 8. The bottom panel shows outcomes in a scenario where oil prices remain at $US100 per barrel and refined product prices remain around current levels over the forecast period. Relative to the central forecasts, the contribution from indirect cost effects related to the conflict in the Middle East are more persistent and contribute to stronger growth in trimmed mean inflation over the forecast period.)
/K 32
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
>>
